      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A charming detached four-bedroom, two-bathroom bungalow set on approximately 0.64 acres, enjoying beautiful maintained gardens and a lovely patio area. The property offers generous outdoor space, privacy and excellent potential for family living. Ideally located within 1km of the local primary school, making it particularly appealing to families.\n\nThe accommodation briefly comprises of a welcoming entrance hallway with tiled flooring, stira to the attic. A lovely cosy sitting room with solid fuel fireplace and two window front aspect. A modern fully fitted kitchen/dining room has a dual aspect and patio doors to the side. Four bedrooms, two with built in wardrobes, the master contains a walk-in wardrobe and ensuite. The main family bathroom is part tiled and contains a three-piece suite.\n\nThe exterior of this home is well maintained with the gardens mainly in lawn, having a selection of fruit trees and shrubberies, patio area to the side off the dining area, tarmac driveway offering ample car parking space.\n\nSuperbly located within 1 km to Killeen primary school, 6km to Granard town for two post-primary schools, crèches and a host of amenities both social and essential, local employers include Pat the Baker, Supervalu, a hardware, credit union, multiple restaurants, hotel and pubs. Granard Area Action Group: A local community development and employment organization involved in local schemes. The Bank (Coworking Space) is located on Market Street. Sporting facilities include Higginstown Sports Complex & Court for tennis and basketball, Granard Greenway, GAA Club, Pitch & Putt, Archery to name a few. Public transport in Granard is serviced by the TFI Local Link Route 865: Operates daily service connecting Lough Gowna, Aughnacliffe, Granard, Ballinalee, Enybegs, and Longford Station/Centre.\n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended.\n\nAccommodation\nEntrance Hall 1.689m x 6.168m (5'6\" x 20'3\"): 0.869m x 11.042m (2'10\" x 36'3\"):\nWelcoming L-shaped entrance hallway with composite front door, two side windows, tiled flooring, hot-press shelved with immersion and light, stira to attic.\n\nSitting Room 4.162m x 3.624m (13'8\" x 11'11\"): \nLovely cosy sitting room with two window front aspect, solid fuel fireplace with timber surround, timber flooring.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room\n6.465m x 3.624m (21'3\" x 11'11\"):\nModern fitted kitchen with wall and floor units offering ample storage space with matching kitchen island, tiled flooring, dual aspect and patio door to the side entrance.\n\nUtility Room 1.690m x 1.862m (5'7\" x 6'1\"):\nFitted units as per the kitchen, tiled flooring and door to the rear garden.\n\nBathroom 2.698m x 1.988m (8'10\" x 6'6\"): \nContains WC, wash hand basin, bath with shower screen and Triton Novel SR unit, heated towel rail window, mirror, part tiled walls and tiled flooring.\n\nBedroom One 2.881m x 2.728m (9'5\" x 8'11\"): \nLaminate flooring, rear aspect, built in wardrobe.\n\nBedroom Two 4.153m x 3.457m (13'8\" x 11'4\"): \nDouble room, timber flooring, two windows front aspect, currently being used as a TV room.\n\nBedroom Three 2.870m x 2.726m (9'5\" x 8'11\"): \nLaminate flooring, rear aspect, built in wardrobe.\n\nBedroom Four 3.725m x 4.259m (12'3\" x 14'): \nLovely spacious master bedroom with dual aspect, laminate flooring, door to the walk-in wardrobe.\n\nWalk in Wardrobe 1.555m x 1.991m (5'1\" x 6'6\"): \nLaminate flooring, light.\n\nEnsuite 2.159m x 1.980m (7'1\" x 6'6\"):\nPart tiled walls, tiled flooring, WC, wash hand basin, shower cubicle, window, heated towel rail, mirror.\n\nSpecial Features & Services\n•Mains water, Septic tank\n•Fibre broadband Sky\n•New hot water cylinder in hot-press\n•Oil Fired Central Heating\n•Solid fuel fireplace in sitting room\n•PVC Double glazed windows & doors\n•Walls pumped, Attic insulated\n•Approx 0.64-acre site\n•Timber Shed, Patio\n•Outside tap and power socket\n•Built circa 2004\n•Approx 137.8 (m2) 1,483 sq.ft\n•PVC facia & soffits\n•Tarmac drive, Footpaths, Well Fenced\n•Ideal family home\n•Turn key finish\n•1km to Killeen primary school\n•6km to Granard town for two post-primary schools\n•11km Edgeworthstown train station\n•8km Killasonna national school\n•Approx 15km to Lough Gowna\n\nIncluded in Sale\n•Washing machine, Dyrer\n•Blinds, Light fittings\n•5 Ring Montpellier electric cooker\n•Integrated fridge\n•Integrated Dishwasher\n•Fixtures & Fittings\n\nBER Details\nBER Rating: C \nBER No. 119662849\n\nDirections\nFrom Granard town take the road for Muckerstaff proceed for approx. 6km and the house is on the left-hand side as indicated by our Sherry FitzGerald Davitt & Davitt For Sale Board Eircode N39 KR59"
